# This file is intentionally (almost) empty.
#
# The app has no environment variables of its own (TAD §0.8):
#
#   - No third-party API keys, ever. The app makes zero calls to Meta, Zoho,
#     GA4, GSC, or LinkedIn — those credentials live only in the Claude Cowork
#     environment that writes public/data/*.json (P2, TASK.md §3).
#
#   - No auth configuration. The MSAL/Entra variables that used to live here
#     (VITE_MSAL_CLIENT_ID, VITE_MSAL_TENANT_ID, VITE_MSAL_REDIRECT_URI,
#     VITE_ALLOWED_EMAILS) were removed by TAD ADR-015: the app no longer
#     authenticates anyone. On launch it asks which role the viewer is
#     operating as, which is a label, not a credential — nothing to configure.
#
#   - No server secrets, because there is no server (TAD ADR-011).
#
# `npm run dev` and `npm run build` both work with no .env.local at all.
#
# If access to the deployment needs to be restricted, that is host-level
# configuration (e.g. Vercel Deployment Protection), not a variable here —
# see TAD §16.4 and BRD §15.2.
